    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Fanconi anemia (FA) is a disorder caused by germline mutations in any one of the FA genes. The FA gene products play an important role in mediating multiple DNA repair pathways. Therefore, FA patients are particularly susceptible to developing squamous cell carcinomas of the head and neck regions (HNSCC), but their hypersensitivity to DNA damaging agents can limit effective treatment with standard radiotherapy due to severe side effects and complications. With the improved survival of FA patients through hematopoietic stem cell transplantation (HSCT), the threat of age-related malignancies such as solid tumor development escalates. Given this increasing risk, there is an unmet clinical need for the development of safe and effective therapies for the treatment of FA related tumors. FLASH radiotherapy (FLASH-RT) is an emerging technology to deliver radiation therapy at an ultra-rapid dose rate. FLASH-RT reduces radiation-induced toxicity to multiple normal tissues while maintaining similar tumor control compared to conventional radiotherapy. However, the potential of FLASH-RT to enhance the therapeutic index of radiotherapy for the treatment of FA related tumors remains unknown. To investigate the efficacy and safety of FLASH-RT for the treatment of HNSCCs in FA patients, we irradiated the oral cavity of mice in a wild type and FA background with either FLASH or conventional radiotherapy (CONV-RT) and compared extent of radiation-induced oral mucositis. We found that FLASH-RT reduced radiation-induced oral mucositis in FANCA deficient mice, while the severity of radiation-induced oral mucositis within the tongue was comparable between FLASH and CONV-irradiated mice in the wild type background. These findings suggest a potential therapeutic benefit with FLASH-RT and hold important clinical implications for the treatment of FANCA deficient patients with HNSCC.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Loo, P. and Rankin, E. (2025). Enhancing the Therapeutic Index of Radiotherapy for the Treatment of Fanconi Anemia Related Squamous Cell Cancers. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/mg541sy0185. https://doi.org/10.25740/mg541sy0185.",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
